  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "9.2.1 - A type mapper defined a dynamic assembly every time it was asked to read or write. Read, Write, GetReader and GetWriter each built a fresh mapper, and with it a fresh code generator, which defines a dynamic assembly of its own; the emitted serialiser was cached on the mapper that was being thrown away, so reusing the type mapper did not help. A caller writing one record at a time built one dynamic assembly per record, until the process ran out of mappings for executable memory and the runtime failed with 'Failed to create RW mapping for RX memory' - a message naming insufficient memory and a Linux kernel limit, neither of which is the cause. The mapper and its generator are now held and reused. Turning optimisation off after a write still stops it emitting, and adding a mapping after a write still takes effect. No API changes.",
